## ===========================================================================
## LORD'S MARKET — Book 4 (`story.ni:4951-5602`), Chapter 2's second half,
## and the Back Alley that ends the chapter (`story.ni:5607`).
##
## The square, its three shops as rooms, the servants and lanterns, and the
## one scripted event of the chapter: Baron Fossville storming out of the
## moneylender's on Jack's first arrival (`EVENT_Fossville`,
## `story.ni:5010-5030`), Gentry's text verbatim — the player's first sight of
## the antagonist. The change document carries it unchanged. The keepers
## (the clothier, Dame Sandler and Pieter, the Chorus Brothers) and their
## stubs arrive with the next increment; the later-visit layers (the sewer,
## Pieter's scene, the clean-Jack shopping) belong to their chapters.
##
## Not carried, noted: the `follow` refusal after the collision (no follow
## action), `enter <storefront>` and the bare `in` (as on Commerce Street).
## ===========================================================================

